  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multimodal models (0.5266 accuracy) outperform RNA-only (0.485) but fusion methods (concat vs weighted) have similar performance. This experiment tests multiprofile data with avgpool aggregation (untested in multimodal setups) to isolate the impact of profile settings and aggregation. It extends the baseline multimodal configuration (config_016) by changing profile_setting from singleprofile to multiprofile, which remains unexplored. This clarifies whether multiprofile data provides incremental value and whether avgpool aggregation improves performance compared to the current None aggregation."
